    {
      "id": 126610,
      "name": "timcarroll",
      "username": "timcarroll",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/439d5e/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2015-01-18T03:29:47.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>It would be great to get an official ruling (and a general flowchart of how certain play actions get resolved). Even after seeing this post, we're still having a debate in our group whether the interpretation is correct.</p><p>The debate generally centers on a couple of different things.</p><p>First, the FAQ has a section that says that a card is still in effect during is destruction, meaning that the card still triggers its power because it is still alive to be triggered by damage.</p><p>The second argument, along the same lines, is that damaging something is a distinct action from destroying it (because among other things, damage can occur and even reduce something to 0 without destroying it, if the right cards are in play.) I think the closest we've got to a definitive ruling here would be the game play for baron blade in the computer game; I believe if you take him out while he has backlash field up, it goes right to end game.</p><p>Anyway, the difference in opinion over these greatly affects the power level of Captain Cosmic.</p><p>Here's a stab at writing these interpretations as a series of steps</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Interpretation 1</p><p>1. Apply damage</p><p>2. Check if target died</p><p>3. If target died, apply any cards or effects based on the cards destruction, and then remove it from play</p><p>4. Apply effects based on the card taking damage.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>interpretation 2</p><p><span>1. Apply damage</span></p><p><span>2.&nbsp;</span><span>Apply effects based on the card taking damage.</span></p><p><span>3. Check if target died</span></p><p><span>4.&nbsp;</span><span>If target died, apply any cards or effects based on the cards destruction, and then remove it from play</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
      "post_number": 3,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:01:05.137Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
