      "id": 126617,
      "name": "seesome",
      "username": "seesome",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/seesome/{size}/2018_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-01-23T18:39:40.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>This came up again last night in a RL game I was playing with AlexxKay. &nbsp;It was frustrating as I was playing Capt Cosmic and kept having constucts wiped out before their \"when damaged\" abilities would have kicked in. &nbsp;However, on reading through the Damage Timing Spreadsheet Alexx linked to, I agree that this makes the most sense. &nbsp;</p><p><span>If destroying a villain target would prevent its \"when damaged\" ability from triggering, I'd be in favor of it, so I suspect my dislike of this is really just that it limited a hero I was playing -- so I just have to suck it up and recognize that being destroyed interrupts a target's ability to use a \"when damaged\" ability (otherwise it would state \"when damaged or destroyed\")</span></p>",
      "post_number": 10,
