    {
      "id": 126619,
      "name": "phantaskippy",
      "username": "phantaskippy",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-01-28T04:23:24.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Both Syphon and Conduit used to have language that it acted when the construct was destroyed, but it actually caused the effect to happen twice in the instance of the construct being destroyed, since the On destruct wording held the card in place while both the damage dealt text and the destruction text activated.</p><p>The wording needed to seperate them into two clauses and put the on-destruct first was just confusing and too wordy.</p><p>It also needed to avoid Captain Cosmic triggering the effects by destroying his own cards, conservation of energy was one of his strongest carsd early on, even after infinite links were gotten rid of, because it coudl trigger Syphon and Conduit and then let you play/draw cards.</p><p>So you are looking at something like:</p><blockquote><p>Play this card next to a hero character card.</p><p>When this card is destroyed by a non-hero card effect that hero may use a power.</p><p>Whenever this card is dealt damage that hero may use a power.</p></blockquote><p>Which is still able to fit on the card, but is wordy and fiddly, and would be the first time on-destruct text would come before other wording that could trigger.</p><p>The effect isn't bad though, and isn't wholly out of sync with the original intent, go with it if you want to.</p>",
      "post_number": 12,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:01:05.798Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 0.0,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 11873,
      "topic_slug": "destroying-constructs-and-getting-benefits",
      "display_username": "phantaskippy",
      "primary_group_name": "playtesters",
      "flair_name": "playtesters",
      "flair_url": "/uploads/default/original/1X/f46928191dbf93b4d0df24571543f49779579225.png",
      "flair_bg_color": "",
      "flair_color": "",
      "flair_group_id": 41,
      "badges_granted": [],
      "version": 1,
      "can_edit": false,
      "can_delete": false,
      "can_recover": false,
      "can_see_hidden_post": false,
      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>Both Syphon and Conduit used to have language that it acted when the construct was destroyed, but it actually caused the effect to happen twice in the instance of the construct being destroyed, since the On destruct wording held the card in place while both the damage dealt text and the destruction text activated.</p><p>The wording needed to seperate them into two clauses and put the on-destruct first was just confusing and too wordy.</p><p>It also needed to avoid Captain Cosmic triggering the effects by destroying his own cards, conservation of energy was one of his strongest carsd early on, even after infinite links were gotten rid of, because it coudl trigger Syphon and Conduit and then let you play/draw cards.</p><p>So you are looking at something like:</p><blockquote><p>Play this card next to a hero character card.</p><p>When this card is destroyed by a non-hero card effect that hero may use a power.</p><p>Whenever this card is dealt damage that hero may use a power.</p></blockquote><p>Which is still able to fit on the card, but is wordy and fiddly, and would be the first time on-destruct text would come before other wording that could trigger.</p><p>The effect isn&#39;t bad though, and isn&#39;t wholly out of sync with the original intent, go with it if you want to.</p>",
